{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wd7krxcu5hcjrtpm4nntosgriquz3eywed5ctwdndoa3eqnri2pq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumeration (definition of done)\nThe whole library in `c_src/` is 3 files: `CMakeLists.txt`, `include/staticloop.h`, `src/staticloop.c` (43 lines). I built the C library with CMake and ran `nm -D`, which showed the **complete** public export surface — no namespace/renaming macros exist in the header:\n\n| Symbol | Signature |\n|---|---|\n| `static_sum` | `int static_sum(int update)` |\n| `driver` | `void driver(int update)` |\n\n## What I wrote (in the current directory, `c_src/` untouched)\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `name = \"StaticLoop\"` so the artifact is `libStaticLoop.so`, matching the C target name.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** (103 lines) — both functions as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\"` with exact C signatures using `std::ffi::{c_char, c_int}`.\n\nFidelity decisions:\n- The function-local `static int sum = 0;` became a crate-level `static mut SUM: c_int` — one shared, non-thread-safe object living for the library's lifetime, exactly like the C original.\n- Arithmetic uses `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_mul` so signed overflow reproduces the C build's two's-complement wrap instead of panicking (no bug \"fixes\" applied).\n- Output goes through the C library's own `printf(\"%d\\n\", ...)` via `unsafe extern \"C\"`, so stdio buffering and interleaving with a caller's own `printf` are identical — `println!` would have used a separate Rust-side buffer and could reorder output.\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not a self-report)\n- `cargo build --release` — succeeds, zero warnings.\n- **Symbol gate:** `diff` of `nm -D --defined-only` name lists between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` is **empty** — both export `T driver` and `T static_sum`.\n- **Differential output test:** a `dlopen` harness exercising `static_sum`/`driver` in interleaved order, including `stride` of `1, 0, -2, 100, INT_MAX, INT_MIN, 715827883` and `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` accumulator overflow → **byte-identical stdout (681 bytes) and stderr**.\n- **Direct-link test:** the same program linked with `-lStaticLoop` against each library → byte-identical (86 bytes), confirming ABI-level drop-in replacement.\n\nOne note for the record: `driver`'s parameter is named `update` in the header but `stride` in the definition. That's a cosmetic C inconsistency only — the ABI signature is the same, and I kept `stride` to match the definition's semantics."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":25890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31c0d202-137a-4ddb-b69d-f166a4019910","uuid":"42703af4-33db-45fe-af58-bc4e4883606b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T19:56:19.903Z"}
